    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow, as the Local Planning Authority, hereby certify that on 14th March 2001, the demolition of existing rear extension and erection of a single storey rear extension of 15.1m2 external floor area and 3m high, would have been lawful within the meaning of sections 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) for the following reason:\r\n\r\nThe extension would fall within Class A, Part 1 Schedule 2 of the General Permitted Development Order 1995.\r\n\r\nInformative: Planning permission is therefore not required.\r\n"
